{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"queryref-publication-repair","children":[{"type":"text","value":"QueryRef publication repair"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pre-repair executable revision: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"536708458"},{"type":"text","value":" on PR #1968.\nRepair executable revision: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"a5fb460d"},{"type":"text","value":".\nGuide revision: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"a1d75726"},{"type":"text","value":".\nEarlier verdicts remain at their recorded revisions in the\n"},{"type":"link","href":"2026-09-30-guide-portfolio-followup.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"portfolio follow-up"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"link","href":"2026-09-30-prep-pr-followup.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"PR preparation follow-up"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Two public laws were promoted from exact expected-failure guards to ordinary\nassertions. Before production edits, the focused run failed two matching\noptimizer aggregate cases, one flat aggregate join, and the initial\ntwo-candidate joined "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"findOne()"},{"type":"text","value":" case. The nonmatching and rejecting aggregate\ncontrols passed. After the repair, the two owners pass 35 tests with no type\nerrors."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Law"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pre-repair gap"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Repair and distinguishing witness"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A computed aggregate projection must join by its published value."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"followRef"},{"type":"text","value":" treated selected "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"total"},{"type":"text","value":" as a source Collection field, so lazy acquisition sought a field that the source rows did not contain. A matching global or flat aggregate QueryRef published no joined row."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Computed projections no longer resolve to a source field. The optimizer owner crosses matching/nonmatching totals with absent, accepting, and rejecting outer predicates and retains a separately materialized aggregate control. The QueryRef owner checks the matching flat aggregate at preload, after the count grows, after a new matching person arrives, and after the count shrinks."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"findOne()"},{"type":"text","value":" QueryRef must reduce to one candidate before its outer join."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"singleResult"},{"type":"text","value":" changed the receiving result shape but did not limit the nested stream. Two initial joined candidates reached the outer query."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The compiler applies a one-row top-K inside the QueryRef, and lazy acquisition treats "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"singleResult"},{"type":"text","value":" as limited. An ordered joined history checks the first, replacement, empty, restored, and changed-join-key cuts. An unordered history checks both QueryRef positions and key-ordered replacement after deletion and reinsertion. A materialized child control checks another receiving boundary."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The pre-repair failures provide hostile controls against the original wrong\ndesigns. The unordered history additionally rejects an ordered-only repair;\nsource updates reject a repair that changes only initial publication. These\ncontrolled Collection histories cover the stated finite rows, join shapes,\nand synchronous public checkpoints. They do not prove all "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"singleResult"},{"type":"text","value":"\nforms, join forms, provider schedules, or unbounded histories. The\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../oracle-coverage.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"coverage map"}]},{"type":"text","value":" assigns those remaining limits to the\nQueryRef and optimizer owners."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"At the repair revision, the DB oracle campaign passed 3,712 tests across 55\nfiles with no type errors. The DB build, edited-file lint, formatting, and\ndocumentation link check passed. The full DB suite passed all 7,861 runtime\ntests across 225 files, then exited with four type-check errors in the\nunchanged "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tests/query/subset-error-matrix.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" fixture. Those type errors\nare outside the QueryRef owners and are not included in a green full-suite\nclaim."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"queryref-publication-repair","text":"QueryRef publication repair","level":1}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"# QueryRef publication repair\n\nPre-repair executable revision: `536708458` on PR #1968.\nRepair executable revision: `a5fb460d`.\nGuide revision: `a1d75726`.\nEarlier verdicts remain at their recorded revisions in the\n[portfolio follow-up](2026-09-30-guide-portfolio-followup.md) and\n[PR preparation follow-up](2026-09-30-prep-pr-followup.md).\n\nTwo public laws were promoted from exact expected-failure guards to ordinary\nassertions. Before production edits, the focused run failed two matching\noptimizer aggregate cases, one flat aggregate join, and the initial\ntwo-candidate joined `findOne()` case. The nonmatching and rejecting aggregate\ncontrols passed. After the repair, the two owners pass 35 tests with no type\nerrors.\n\n| Law | Pre-repair gap | Repair and distinguishing witness |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| A computed aggregate projection must join by its published value. | `followRef` treated selected `total` as a source Collection field, so lazy acquisition sought a field that the source rows did not contain. A matching global or flat aggregate QueryRef published no joined row. | Computed projections no longer resolve to a source field. The optimizer owner crosses matching/nonmatching totals with absent, accepting, and rejecting outer predicates and retains a separately materialized aggregate control. The QueryRef owner checks the matching flat aggregate at preload, after the count grows, after a new matching person arrives, and after the count shrinks. |\n| A `findOne()` QueryRef must reduce to one candidate before its outer join. | `singleResult` changed the receiving result shape but did not limit the nested stream. Two initial joined candidates reached the outer query. | The compiler applies a one-row top-K inside the QueryRef, and lazy acquisition treats `singleResult` as limited. An ordered joined history checks the first, replacement, empty, restored, and changed-join-key cuts. An unordered history checks both QueryRef positions and key-ordered replacement after deletion and reinsertion. A materialized child control checks another receiving boundary. |\n\nThe pre-repair failures provide hostile controls against the original wrong\ndesigns. The unordered history additionally rejects an ordered-only repair;\nsource updates reject a repair that changes only initial publication. These\ncontrolled Collection histories cover the stated finite rows, join shapes,\nand synchronous public checkpoints. They do not prove all `singleResult`\nforms, join forms, provider schedules, or unbounded histories. The\n[coverage map](../oracle-coverage.md) assigns those remaining limits to the\nQueryRef and optimizer owners.\n\nAt the repair revision, the DB oracle campaign passed 3,712 tests across 55\nfiles with no type errors. The DB build, edited-file lint, formatting, and\ndocumentation link check passed. The full DB suite passed all 7,861 runtime\ntests across 225 files, then exited with four type-check errors in the\nunchanged `tests/query/subset-error-matrix.test.ts` fixture. Those type errors\nare outside the QueryRef owners and are not included in a green full-suite\nclaim.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"# QueryRef publication repair\n\nPre-repair executable revision: `536708458` on PR #1968.\nRepair executable revision: `a5fb460d`.\nGuide revision: `a1d75726`.\nEarlier verdicts remain at their recorded revisions in the\n[portfolio follow-up](2026-09-30-guide-portfolio-followup.md) and\n[PR preparation follow-up](2026-09-30-prep-pr-followup.md).\n\nTwo public laws were promoted from exact expected-failure guards to ordinary\nassertions. Before production edits, the focused run failed two matching\noptimizer aggregate cases, one flat aggregate join, and the initial\ntwo-candidate joined `findOne()` case. The nonmatching and rejecting aggregate\ncontrols passed. After the repair, the two owners pass 35 tests with no type\nerrors.\n\n| Law | Pre-repair gap | Repair and distinguishing witness |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| A computed aggregate projection must join by its published value. | `followRef` treated selected `total` as a source Collection field, so lazy acquisition sought a field that the source rows did not contain. A matching global or flat aggregate QueryRef published no joined row. | Computed projections no longer resolve to a source field. The optimizer owner crosses matching/nonmatching totals with absent, accepting, and rejecting outer predicates and retains a separately materialized aggregate control. The QueryRef owner checks the matching flat aggregate at preload, after the count grows, after a new matching person arrives, and after the count shrinks. |\n| A `findOne()` QueryRef must reduce to one candidate before its outer join. | `singleResult` changed the receiving result shape but did not limit the nested stream. Two initial joined candidates reached the outer query. | The compiler applies a one-row top-K inside the QueryRef, and lazy acquisition treats `singleResult` as limited. An ordered joined history checks the first, replacement, empty, restored, and changed-join-key cuts. An unordered history checks both QueryRef positions and key-ordered replacement after deletion and reinsertion. A materialized child control checks another receiving boundary. |\n\nThe pre-repair failures provide hostile controls against the original wrong\ndesigns. The unordered history additionally rejects an ordered-only repair;\nsource updates reject a repair that changes only initial publication. These\ncontrolled Collection histories cover the stated finite rows, join shapes,\nand synchronous public checkpoints. They do not prove all `singleResult`\nforms, join forms, provider schedules, or unbounded histories. The\n[coverage map](../oracle-coverage.md) assigns those remaining limits to the\nQueryRef and optimizer owners.\n\nAt the repair revision, the DB oracle campaign passed 3,712 tests across 55\nfiles with no type errors. The DB build, edited-file lint, formatting, and\ndocumentation link check passed. The full DB suite passed all 7,861 runtime\ntests across 225 files, then exited with four type-check errors in the\nunchanged `tests/query/subset-error-matrix.test.ts` fixture. Those type errors\nare outside the QueryRef owners and are not included in a green full-suite\nclaim.\n"}
